internal/oracle/testdata/rest_parameter_relation/n01_listener_needs_a_field_it_isnt_handed.a:8:26: Adamic 0.1 refuses a function taking { text: string; code: number; } seen as one taking { text: string; } (tsc relates a method's parameters both ways), so it can be handed what it can't take; write the method as a property holding a function (handle: (animal: Animal) => void), which tsc checks one way, or take the wider type in the method (method-signature-style)
